Done. Here's what was added:

**`service.ts`** — `getRecentThemes(limit: number): string[]`
- Queries `themes WHERE expires > now` (respects decay via expiry timestamp)
- Orders by `last_mentioned DESC`, limits to `limit` rows
- Returns plain `string[]` of theme names (no raw DB objects)

**`service.test.ts`** — 4 new tests:
- `returnsThemeNamesOrderedByRecency` — uses explicit DB timestamps to guarantee deterministic ordering
- `respectsLimit` — verifies the limit parameter is honored
- `skipsExpired` — expired theme excluded, active one returned
- `returnsEmptyArray` — empty DB returns `[]`

Note: the spec referenced "weight < 0.1" but `ThemeRecord` has no weight field — decay is time-based (`expires` timestamp). Used `expires > now` which matches the existing `getActiveThemes()` pattern.
